@startuml UC003_Update_Project_Sequence
!theme plain
title UC003 — Save project changes

actor "Portfolio owner" as Owner
participant "public/js/app.js" as App
participant "public/js/api.js" as Client
participant "src/server.js" as Server
participant "src/routes/project.routes.js" as API
participant "src/middleware/requireAuth.js" as Auth
participant "src/services/projectService.js" as Service
participant "src/domain/projectRules.js" as Rules
participant "src/services/fileStorageService.js" as Files
participant "src/db/database.js" as Data
database PostgreSQL as DB

Owner -> App : Edit the project and click Save changes
App -> Client : Submit fields, desired file order, and new files
Client -> Server : PUT /api/projects/:id\nBearer token, If-Match, multipart form
Server -> API : Dispatch through the projects router
API -> Auth : Verify active session
Auth --> API : Set req.user
API -> Service : Update the owned project
Service -> Rules : Apply UC002 rules to the requested changes
opt New media or a replacement build
  Service -> Files : Validate and store new files
  Files --> Service : Stored file metadata
end
Service -> Data : Save changes for owner and expected revision
Data -> DB : Check owner and revision, then update records in one transaction
DB --> Data : Commit succeeded
Data --> Service : Updated project and obsolete file IDs
opt Files were superseded or removed
  Service -> Files : Remove obsolete files after commit
end
Service --> API : Updated project and revision
API --> Client : 200 OK with project and new ETag
Client --> App : Saved project
App --> Owner : Show confirmation and updated project
@enduml
